<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Cook</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 10), Druid (guild level 18)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cook &lt;food&gt;
</pre>
<p>Builds a small campfire and cooks a piece of food on it: meat from
butchering, a fish, a plant. Cooked food fills you more, and cooking burns
away some of any poison in it; a weak poison is gone altogether. Food can
be cooked only once.
</p><p>You need open ground for a fire: not in a city or indoors, not on water,
and not on snow or ice. Your skill and your dexterity decide whether you
find enough to start a fire, and some lands give less kindling than others.
If a campfire is already burning, you cook on it without building another.
Each try takes 20 endurance, and you need at least that much; you can't cook
while fighting. Practising it needs brain 10.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
